course: dictionary
lesson: 8928
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word sign is a good example. A road sign is a board with words or pictures, but a sign in maths is a mark like + or =. The meaning that fits depends on the words around it, which is its context.
explain: «Pain is a warning sign, so take breaks and stop if it hurts.» Here sign does not mean a board. A warning sign is something that shows a problem may be coming. Try your meaning in the sentence: "pain is a warning that..." makes sense, so you know you have the right meaning.
explain: Sign can also be a verb, a word for an action. To sign is to write your name on something, and it is also to talk with your hands. «British Sign Language (BSL) is a full language with its own grammar, different from English.» Here sign language is a language made with hand shapes.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: One word can have several meanings, so check which one fits the sentence.
fact: «Sign» as a noun can be a board with words or pictures, a maths mark, or something that shows something is true or will happen.
fact: «Sign» as a verb means to write your name on something, or to talk with hand signs.
fact: «Heat exhaustion» can turn into heatstroke, so one warning sign is that a hot person stops sweating.
exercise: «Heat exhaustion can turn into heatstroke, so one warning sign is that a hot person stops sweating.» What does sign mean here? | A maths mark like + or = | To write your name | A board with words on the road | *Something that shows a problem is happening
exercise: In the number sentence 5 + 3 = 8, what is the + called? | A picture | A number | A word | *A sign
exercise: «British Sign Language (BSL) uses hand shapes, movements, the face and the body.» What is BSL made from? | Coloured pencils | Only spoken sounds | Only written words | *Hand shapes, movements, the face and the body
test: «Pain is a warning sign, so take breaks and stop if it hurts.» What does sign mean in this sentence? | A maths mark | To write your name | *Something that shows a problem may come | A board with words
test: «Her broken-spear drawing becomes the sign for la.» Which word means a picture or hand shape that stands for a word? | Spear | *Sign | Broken | Drawing
exam: Which sentence uses sign as a verb, meaning to write your name? | A plus sign is +. | The road sign says STOP. | Dark clouds are a sign of rain. | *Please sign your name at the bottom.
